   "file": "TauCeti/Probability/Process/TimeMeasure.lean",
   "fix": "Add one lemma, e.g. `comap_coe_volume_Ioc (a b : \u211d\u22650) : Measure.comap ((\u2191) : \u211d\u22650 \u2192 \u211d) volume (Ioc a b) = ENNReal.ofReal (b - a)`, proved once by `comap_apply`/`image_coe_Ioc`/`volume_Ioc`. Then prove `timeMeasure_Ioc` and `timeMeasure_univ` with `simp [timeMeasure_def, Ioc_inter_Ioc, comap_coe_volume_Ioc]` or a single `rw`.",
   "issue": "`timeMeasure_Ioc` uses a seven-step `rw` chain of named lemmas (`restrict_apply`, `Ioc_inter_Ioc`, `max_eq_left`, `comap_apply`, `NNReal.image_coe_Ioc`, `Real.volume_Ioc`). The same comap/image/volume segment is repeated in `timeMeasure_univ` (line 47). A Mathlib rename would break both, and the shared fact (the pulled-back Lebesgue measure of `Ioc a b` in `\u211d\u22650`) is not exposed.",
